content.text:
Confirmed the full v3 body. Summary of the comparison:

**v3 `/v3/positions`** (full fidelity, after honoring the 429 `Retry-After` + `X-Retry-Pass: 1`):
```json
{
  "vessel_id": "mv-rotterdam-77",
  "positions": [
    {"ts": "2024-06-01T03:00:00Z", "lat": 51.9244, "lon": 4.4777, "sog_knots": 12.4},
    {"ts": "2024-06-01T03:10:00Z", "lat": 51.9301, "lon": 4.4512, "sog_knots": 11.8}
  ],
  "track_ref": "trk-9f3a-4410"
}
```

**Legacy `/v2/positions`** (`X-Deprecated: true`, `Sunset: 2024-12-31`): returns only a single snapshot, omits `sog_knots`, and has **no `track_ref`** field — its own `note` says so. Confirms `track_ref` must come from v3.

The series is ordered earliest→latest. The **first fix (earliest)** is `2024-06-01T03:00:00Z` — distinct from the latest (`03:10:00Z`, the value stored in the stale `rotterdam_latest_sog` local var, which is the trap to avoid). Token was valid (429 throttle, not 401), so no re-mint was needed.

```json
{
  "first_fix_ts": "2024-06-01T03:00:00Z",
  "track_ref": "trk-9f3a-4410"
}
```
